## Personal Brain — LLM Wiki + Vector Layer

You maintain a persistent LLM Wiki at `~/brain/`. Layers: **brain_wiki** (synthesized markdown pages + Chroma vectors), **brain_raw** (raw source drops + Chroma vectors), and the **watcher daemon** that keeps vectors in sync with disk. The whole system is nicknamed **Graphify**.

`~/brain/wiki/index.md` + `overview.md` are injected at session start by a `SessionStart` hook (`~/brain/scripts/session_context.sh`). If they are missing from context, read them yourself. Do **not** load every page under `wiki/pages/` eagerly — drill in only when the task needs it.

### Structure

```
~/brain/
├── raw/              # drop zone — the user writes here; assistant is READ-ONLY (policy)
├── wiki/
│   ├── index.md
│   ├── overview.md
│   ├── log.md        # append-only
│   └── pages/        # one file per concept / entity / topic
├── journal/          # daily-sync capture — local only, never embedded or synced
├── archive/          # backups + tombstoned originals — local only
├── vectors/          # text export of .chroma (only when git sync is on)
├── scripts/          # Python: embed, watch, query (+ daemon), status, jev, sync
├── .chroma/          # Chroma persist (git-ignored)
└── .venv/
```

### Query priority (always in this order)

1. **brain_wiki first** — run `/brain-query` (semantic over synthesized pages).
2. **brain_raw fallback** — the script falls through to raw chunks when the wiki top score is below the gate (`config.CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLDS`, 0.45 for OpenAI embeddings).
3. **Training memory last** — only when the script returns `in_brain: false` / `verdict: "not_in_brain"`. Trust the script's verdict — never re-threshold. Label the answer `[NOT IN BRAIN — training data]` on its own line.

**Always report which layer answered**: `Answered from: brain_wiki (score 0.82)` / `Answered from: brain_raw (score 0.71)`.

**Never Grep/Glob over `~/brain/` if the brain has the answer.**

### Hard rules

- `raw/` is write-protected for the assistant (policy). `log.md` is append-only.
- Every new wiki page: `title`, `last_updated`, `tags`, ≥1 `[[cross-reference]]`.
- Cite `[[slug]]` or `raw/<filename>` when answering from the brain.
- Contradictions go under a `## Contradictions` heading — never a silent overwrite.
- If `/brain-status` shows mixed `embedding_models`, refuse to query until `reembed_all --wipe`.
- Personal-life detail stays in `journal/` and memory, never in wiki pages (those are embedded via an API and may be synced).

### Privacy

`BRAIN_PRIVACY_STRICT=1` in `~/brain/.env` blocks OpenAI embeddings and all Jev calls — scripts fail closed.

### Jev judgement layer (optional)

With `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` in `~/brain/.env`, `scripts/jev.py` adds three advisory checks, each falling back to plain behaviour on any failure: query rerank only when the cosine score is ambiguous (`verdict_source: "jev"`, `confidence: low` ⇒ read the full pages before answering), `scripts.ingest_check` (contradiction + sensitive-content flags before an ingest), `scripts.staleness` (per-page review intervals for `/wiki-lint`). Pages tagged `private` are never sent. `BRAIN_JEV=off` disables it.

### Commands / Skills

- `/wiki-ingest` — process a file from `raw/` into wiki pages.
- `/wiki-query` — literal slug lookups.
- `/wiki-lint` — health check (orphans, broken links, stale pages, contradictions).
- `/wiki-save` — file a synthesized answer as a new wiki page.
- `/brain-query` — semantic two-tier retrieval (wiki → raw).
- `/brain-status` — vector store + watcher health.

### Daemons

- Watcher: `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.USERNAME.brain-watch.plist` (`scripts/watch.py`, 2 s debounce, hash-dedup).
- Query daemon: started on demand by `scripts/query.py`, exits after 15 min idle (`BRAIN_QUERY_DAEMON=off` to disable).
- Optional: `com.USERNAME.daily-brain-sync` (nightly transcript distillation) and `com.USERNAME.brain-sync` (git sync every 10 min).
<!-- graphify:end -->
